   "evidence": "Proof body at Conjugate.lean:527-532 uses only `MulAut.conjNormal_apply`, `group`, `Module.End.mul_apply`, `map_mul`. Conjugate.lean:8-10 imports `Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Skeletal` / `TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.Induction.Restriction`, and Restriction.lean:8-10 imports `TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.CharacterTable.ClassFunction`, `Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Irreducible`, `Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Rep.Res`. Normal.lean:8 is `import TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.Induction.Conjugate`, used only at Normal.lean:60.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Induction/Conjugate.lean",
   "fix": "Put the lemma in an early lightweight module \u2014 e.g. a new `TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/ConjNormal.lean` importing only `Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic` and `Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.ConjAct` \u2014 and have `Induction/Conjugate.lean`, `Induction/Clifford/Basic.lean` and `LinearAlgebra/Eigenspace/JointEigenvector/Normal.lean` import that instead. `Clifford/Basic.lean` then keeps its `ConjAct` import and needs no edge to `Conjugate.lean`; `Normal.lean` needs no `TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.Induction.*` import at all (`Representation.apply_bijective` is `Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Basic.lean:107`).",
   "issue": "`TauCeti.Representation.apply_conjNormal_inv` is `\u03c1 g (\u03c1 (g\u207b\u00b9 n g) v) = \u03c1 n (\u03c1 g v)`, provable from `Representation` + `MulAut.conjNormal` alone, but it is placed in `Induction/Conjugate.lean`, whose imports (lines 8-10) pull in `Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Skeletal`, `Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Rep.Res`, `Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Irreducible`, `Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Character` and `TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.CharacterTable.ClassFunction`. Consequences in this PR: `TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Eigenspace/JointEigenvector/Normal.lean:8` imports that entire stack solely for this identity, and `TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Induction/Clifford/Basic.lean:10` gains a dependency on `Conjugate.lean` it did not previously have (the diff drops the lightweight `Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.ConjAct` for it).",
   "line": 527
  }
